#====================================================================
# E327 - Materialize dependency-owned resources when links are forbidden
#====================================================================

id:                     E362
trigger_tool:           conan|package|test_package
phase:                  packaging|validation
error_signature:        PermissionError.*os.symlink|Permission denied.*symlink|missing packaged resource.*link|dangling symbolic link

severity:               2
category:               hmdfs, conan, packaging, symlink, resource-layout
match_keywords:         Conan dependency, shared template, symlink, no-link, HMDFS, materialize, byte compare, resource identity, package_folder
title:                  Materialize dependency-owned resources when the target filesystem forbids links

root_cause:             An upstream resource package may install relative links to files owned by another runtime package. Archive extraction or package copy can omit dangling links, while explicit symlink creation can be rejected by the target filesystem. Blindly copying similarly named local files loses the ownership contract and can silently package stale or unrelated content.
affected_scope:         Conan packages whose upstream resource layout links to files supplied by a declared dependency, when the target package filesystem cannot preserve or create those links.
verification_cmd:       Resolve the exact dependency node from self.dependencies, materialize each required resource into the consumer package as a regular file, reject missing source resources, then compare every installed file byte-for-byte with its dependency-owned source in test_package.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           dependency-derived-resource-materialization
rec_description:        Keep the upstream public filename, but derive the source path from the exact Conan dependency package_folder. Copy each dependency-owned target as a regular file during package(), fail if the source does not exist, and expose no machine-specific cache path. In test_package, require a regular non-link file and compare its complete bytes with the same resolved dependency source. Validate the full expected resource inventory separately.
rec_command:            |
  dependency_root = self.dependencies["<dependency>"].package_folder
  # Map each upstream linked name to its dependency-owned source.
  # copy(..., keep_path=False) into the package public resource directory.
  # In test_package: test -f "$dst" && test ! -L "$dst" && cmp -s "$src" "$dst"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-package-resource-map-and-consumer-identity-test

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      preserve-links-on-capable-filesystem
fallback_description:   Preserve the upstream relative links only when the packaging and runtime filesystems both support them and the installed dependency layout makes every target resolvable. Still validate targets and inventory from a clean package.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       os\.symlink|ln -s
forbid_1_reason:        Recreating links does not solve a filesystem policy that rejects link creation and may fail late in package().
forbid_1_consequence:   The package build fails or produces missing public resources.

forbid_2_pattern:       (\.conan2|storage/Users|package_folder).*hard.?cod|copy.*source_folder.*shared
forbid_2_reason:        Hard-coded cache paths or unrelated source-tree copies are not bound to the dependency revision selected by Conan.
forbid_2_consequence:   A fresh cache can package stale or ABI-incompatible resource content.

forbid_3_pattern:       exists.*only|test -f.*without.*cmp|skip.*content
forbid_3_reason:        Existence alone cannot prove that materialization preserved the dependency-owned resource contract.
forbid_3_consequence:   Empty, stale, or wrongly mapped resources can pass the consumer test.

doc_file: doc/E362.md
similar_to: E292, E274, E316
last_updated:           2026-08-16
source_event:           acf-openssh 0.11.2 materialized three acf-core templates after HMDFS omitted or rejected the upstream relative links

authors: wxjshr <wxjshr@noreply.gitcode.com>
source_pr: !5414
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.8
